      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T04:40:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m concerned about overloading the user stopped/started notifications like this.  The users are never actually stopped from an Android system perspective.  Things quickly get very confusing when user stop/start can mean two different things, a real stop/start or a fake one.\n\nWhat are the exact actions that vold and storaged take in \"onUserStarted\" and \"onUserStopped\"?  I wonder if these methods need to be renamed to something more focused on storage that isn\u0027t borrowed from the user lifecycle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7f993c2_83c7999e",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T07:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The goal is destroy the emulated volumes for the old primary volume and re-create and mount the emulated volumes for the new primary volume.\n\nThis follows the same approach as `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` [https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java;l\u003d1142?q\u003dresetIfBootedAndConnected\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain]. The difference is we aren\u0027t resetting vold and informing vold about the users present (which is adding users to vold), we are just stopping and starting from vold \u0026 storaged standpoint.\n\nAnd `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` is called in various scenarios other than user start and stop such as `setPrimaryStorageUuid`, `mount`, `forgetVolume` \u0026 `StorageManagerInternal#resetUser`",
      "parentUuid": "28ee4bdf_8707455a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "388bfba6_439863a5",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-09T04:22:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then perhaps the problem is that `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` needs to be called in some case when currently it isn\u0027t?  I\u0027m not an expert on this part of the code, so please take my opinion with a grain of salt, but I get the impression that that would solve the problem in a simpler way.  How is your solution better?",
      "parentUuid": "c7f993c2_83c7999e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e554f936_d4d75372",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-09T04:41:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, if we just call `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` after move storage then the solution becomes simpler.\n\n`resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` resets *everything* from vold including disks, volumes and user states and re-creates them again by calling the user lifecycle methods again for unlocked users\n\nMy implementation does only a subset of the tasks required to remount the emulated volumes after move. (i.e., stop user and start user) which will create and mount the correct emulated volumes back.",
      "parentUuid": "388bfba6_439863a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab0aa2de_fe103a1a",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T18:35:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After the move operation, the current user\u0027s emulated volume gets mounted again from vold (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/vold/MoveStorage.cpp;l\u003d226-230) as emulated volume\u0027s UUID is being used to execute the move.\n\nThe reset operation will (as stated earlier) will remove everything by calling `IVold#reset` (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/refs/heads/main:system/vold/VolumeManager.cpp;l\u003d904) which includes all the emulated volumes and destroys and re-creates the disk.\n\nThen after that, it will add back the users and starts the already started users known by StorageManagerService. This starting of user also mounts the emulated volumes for the user (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/vold/VolumeManager.cpp;l\u003d459)\n\nThis CL remounts the emulated volumes for background users for which are currently running (or have emulated volumes mounted for them) by stopping the user (which unmounts the emulated volumes) and starting the user back again (which mounts the correct emulated volumes).\n\nThis difference between this CL and calling `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` is that this solution only does the operations that are required to remount the emulated volumes while `resetIfRebootedAndConnected()` does the *full* reset\n\nPlease let me know your thoughts on this.",
      "parentUuid": "e554f936_d4d75372",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "691f753b_b96bf786",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T18:48:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that the full reset does more work.  What I am looking for is an explanation for why the full reset is not appropriate to use in this context.  Moving apps between internal and adoptable storage is a rare operation, so I would assume that it doesn\u0027t need to be super well optimized.  It might be the case that doing some unnecessary work is justified by simplicity of implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "ab0aa2de_fe103a1a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de1ab4f1_00664a50",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1386,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T18:55:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use-case we are trying to solve here is not for moving apps, it is for changing the primary storage, which moves the content to adoptable storage from internal or vice versa.\n\nI agree full reset will solve the problem, but we have to decide if we want to all the work or just do the required part.\n\nPlease let me know your thoughts.",
      "parentUuid": "691f753b_b96bf786",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1385,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 1386,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "b9d6c6f900e3611dd3f11f2b91a6b3a28406297b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
